# Corpus unit mechanistic-understanding/C02 — gap (variance mandatory in policy, optional in
# the annotation)
#
# Source: m0/annotations/mechanistic-understanding.yaml C02 (causal, controlled_comparison;
# corpus pin 62e9b54). Headline: subtracting a toxic vector (wtoxic, mlp_v19, or svd_utoxic0)
# from the last-layer residual stream drops Perspective toxicity below the No Op baseline
# (0.453 -> 0.245/0.305/0.268) while preserving language quality — perplexity 23.30-23.56
# (comparable to DPO 23.34) and F1 0.192-0.193 (comparable to No Op 0.193) (E02, Table 2).
#
# Lowering notes (conventions: corpus-units/LOWERING.md):
#   * The causal claim lowers as a controlled comparison of the intervention against the No Op
#     baseline: better(subtract_toxic, no_op, toxicity_at_matched_ppl, gpt2_medium). Q folds the
#     quality-preservation constraint (comparison held at DPO-matched perplexity) into one
#     constant; the three vectors and the F1/ppl cells stay in nl and refs.
#   * Policy-vs-annotation divergence, recorded per the uniform-standard rule: the annotator
#     rated the seeds/variance CQ OPTIONAL and unmet ("effect-vs-noise is asserted, not shown"),
#     but corpus-v1 makes variance_reported mandatory family-wide (27 mandatory vs 16 optional
#     annotations corpus-wide), and the policy call wins. E02 runs a single generation pass over
#     1,199 prompts with no seeds or variance in Metrics, so variance_reported has no honest
#     leaf. An open mandatory obligation is an IncompleteArgument rejection, so no complete
#     controlled_comparison is declarable — E2-style gap on empty complete support
#     (adaptive-pruning/C03 pattern).
#   * baseline_parity (No Op scored under identical decoding) and measurement_validity (alpha
#     calibrated to DPO perplexity, NOT to the toxicity outcome; quality checked on both fluency
#     and content-overlap axes) are annotated met and kept as leaves.
#
# Expected verdict is at the bottom of this file (golden oracle).

artifact mechanistic-understanding at sha256:04b48a8cb1d4
policy corpus-v1
use backends [nd@1]

# --- The headline claim, not assemblable at corpus-v1's evidential bar --------------------------

claim c02
  nl      = "Subtracting a toxic vector (wtoxic, mlp_v19, or svd_utoxic0) from the last-layer residual stream reduces Perspective toxicity below No Op (0.453 -> 0.245/0.305/0.268) while preserving quality at DPO-matched perplexity (ppl 23.30-23.56 vs DPO 23.34; F1 ~0.193)"
  formal  = better(subtract_toxic, no_op, toxicity_at_matched_ppl, gpt2_medium)
  binding = { author = m0-annotator, audit-status = unreviewed }

# --- Evidence leaves are present ... ------------------------------------------------------------

# Principal premise: Table 2's per-vector toxicity/ppl/F1 cells against the No Op row, per
# result cell, folded into refs.
leaf e1 : reports(e02, compares(subtract_toxic, no_op, toxicity_at_matched_ppl, gpt2_medium, favorable))
  kind       = observed
  provenance = ai-executed
  refs       = [evidence/tables/table2_interventions_results.md, evidence/tables/table3_topk_continuations.md, trace/exploration_tree.yaml#N07]

leaf e2 : matched_setup(subtract_toxic, no_op, e02)
  kind       = attested
  provenance = ai-executed
  refs       = [logic/experiments.md#E02-Baselines, evidence/tables/table2_interventions_results.md]

leaf e3 : valid_measurement(toxicity_at_matched_ppl, e02)
  kind       = attested
  provenance = ai-executed
  refs       = [logic/experiments.md#E02-Procedure-step-3, logic/experiments.md#E02-Procedure-steps-5-6]

# --- ... but no complete argument is declarable -------------------------------------------------

# (Intentionally no `arg`: variance_reported(e02) has no honest leaf — E02 is a single
# generation pass with no seeds or uncertainty — and corpus-v1 makes that obligation mandatory,
# though the annotator rated it optional. The claim's complete-support set is therefore empty.)

status c02

